cells.Treatment / Management:
Viral: supportive (NSAIDs, saline, decongestants); 

Bacterial: amox-clav 1st line, doxy if PCN allergy;

 ENT referral if persistent (after 2nd course of abx)  or severe, or immunocomp with suspected fungal 

Hospitalize if IV antibiotics & surgical consult

cells.Clinical Presentation:
Viral: watery discharge, preauricular lymph nodes; tearing, photophobia,  

Bacterial: thick purulent discharge, lids stuck AM; 

Allergic: bilateral itching, watery/stringy discharge

cells.Etiology:
EBV, saliva spread;
Incubation for 4-6 weeks 
Self-limited and benign
